.TH hsh

.SH NAME
.B hsh
hsh - simple UNIX command interpreter

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hsh
Program is a simple command line interpreter. Executing commans read from stnadard input. Program mimics behaviour of .B/bin/sh for basic command execution.

.SH BUILD
Developed using C programming language.

.SH INTERACTIVE MODE
Standard output is connected to terminal, by display the prompt:

.PP
$

.PP
The user enters commands, which get parsed & executed. Shell waits for each command to finish before displaying the next prompt. ($)

.SH NON-INTERACTIVE MODE
Input piped/redirected, shell reads commmands until EOF & executes each in order.

.PP
echo "la -l" | hsh

.SH BUILTINS
.TP
.B exit [stat]
Exit the shell if numberic stat is provided, shell exits with that stat otherwise, exits with stat 0.

.TP
.B env
Print current encironment variables.

